; Outside runtest: a test run cannot hold a real model's weights, a 4 GiB
; file or a corpus.
;
; TESSERA's medium student (84 MB) against torch.load's reading of it. Run it
; with
;   NX_IO_PT_CKPT=student_medium.pt NX_IO_PT_REF=reference.npz \
;   dune exec packages/nx/test/io/weights/test_pytorch_weights.exe
; where reference.npz holds, for each tensor torch.load reads under a path of
; string keys and indices, its bytes at uint8 with a last axis of its element's
; bytes, named by the path, and its dtype's name under the path and ".dtype".
;
; TESSERA's 2B teacher (8.26 GB), whose entries past 4 GiB have ZIP64 data
; descriptors. Run it with
;   NX_IO_PT_TEACHER=tessera_v2_2B_teacher.pt \
;   dune exec packages/nx/test/io/weights/test_pytorch_teacher.exe
;
; Zip entries of 0xFFFFFFFF bytes in sparse 4 GiB files, which take that much
; address space and no disk. Run it with
;   dune exec packages/nx/test/io/weights/test_zip_boundary.exe

;
; The IETF FLAC test files whole, 296 MB: every file a decoder must read
; against the MD5 its encoder stated, every other refused. Run it with
;   NX_IO_FLAC_TESTS=flac-test-files \
;   dune exec packages/nx/test/io/weights/test_flac_corpus.exe
; where flac-test-files is https://github.com/ietf-wg-cellar/flac-test-files
; at aa7b0c6cf32994c106ae517a08134c28a96ff5b2, holding subset/, uncommon/
; and faulty/.
;
; LibriSpeech files against libsndfile's int16 reading. Run it with
;   NX_IO_LIBRISPEECH=LibriSpeech NX_IO_LIBRISPEECH_LIST=list.tsv \
;   dune exec packages/nx/test/io/weights/test_librispeech.exe
; where list.tsv has a header line, then for each file its path under
; LibriSpeech, its rate, its rows and the BLAKE2b-256 of its samples as
; little-endian int16, as soundfile reads them.
;
; A WAV save past 4 GiB, which writes RF64. It writes 4 GiB to disk, a WAV
; file being no sparse file, and skips unless the directory's file system
; has 50 GiB free past that. Run it with
;   NX_IO_RF64_DIR=dir dune exec packages/nx/test/io/weights/test_rf64.exe

(executables
 (names
  test_pytorch_weights
  test_pytorch_teacher
  test_zip_boundary
  test_flac_corpus
  test_librispeech
  test_rf64)
 (libraries nx nx_array nx_io unix windtrap))
